+# Projection concurrence Site release — 24 October 2026
+
+Scope: independent image-space teaching mode linked from the shadow workbench. The sculpture solver, transcript, accepted-decryption module, manual fold model and entrance model are unchanged. Eight exact research fixtures are preserved with source hashes; eleven supplementary local wrong-pick/shared-bias fixtures are independently compared. There is no real-monument fit or K4 trial.
+
+Implemented: normalized line-scatter eigenvector fit, conditioning and invalid-geometry handling; eight synthetic presets; finite-image intersection controls; reproducible added noise and small held-out wrong pick; separate declared pick uncertainty; training/held-out inspection; clipped predicted lines without clipping coordinates; infinity/off-screen labels; native-pixel line residuals and explicitly endpoint-only standardized residuals; full JSON export. No probability or scientific acceptance verdict is shown.
+
+Interpretation: a predicted line does not supply a ground point or depth. Coincident lines are nonunique; parallel distinct lines are valid at image infinity. Two lines alone are not an overidentifying test. Finite versus infinite IMAGE intersections do not identify physical source distance/type. Low residuals do not certify match identity, 3D concurrence, sunlight, date, north or K4 information.
+
+Photo: exact 1580×2000 public LOC derivative was successfully materialized through the supported Library workflow after one authorized retry with public-provenance evidence. SHA-256 cab93103a992620c5d20fa426c77468d70ec83197ab8a1c7484d790f4354c50d verified; actual pixels inspected. Credit and LOC record are visible. It shows apertures and illuminated paving, with zero certified pair matches. No fitted rays are drawn. The separately denied metadata ZIP was not retried or used; no incomplete annotations were reconstructed. Photo provenance is recorded in projection-test/photo-provenance.json.
+
+QA: focused numerical fixtures, supplementary endpoint residuals, invalid-input preservation, deterministic controls, real module handlers, captured JSON Blob roundtrip, line clipping and mode-navigation tests. Full suite results are recorded with the release response. Responsive CSS and a 390×844 / 768×1024 same-origin iframe fixture are supplied at qa/projection-mobile.html. These structural checks do not establish actual rendered layout.
+
+Actual browser limitation: supported CUA inventory on the connected Mac reported the Mac locked and returned no app/browser surfaces. No unlock bypass or alternative browser-control route was attempted. Desktop/mobile rendered QA and browser download verification remain unperformed in this executor. Parent can review the published normal route and narrow-layout fixture in its supported browser. This is distinct from successful automated validation and native deployment verification.
